Omarchy is an opinionated, keyboard-driven desktop built on the Hyprland
Wayland compositor and a Quickshell bar, launcher, and control panels. It
ships a curated set of themes that restyle the whole desktop at once, a menu
system for setup and maintenance, and defaults for terminals, editors, and
common tools.

This port installs the Omarchy runtime with a FreeBSD compatibility layer:
package management through pkg(8), boot environments through bectl(8),
session services under daemon(8) in place of systemd user units, and
backlight(8), acpiconf(8), sysctl(8), and ifconfig(8) in place of Linux
sysfs and NetworkManager. For the complete desktop as the Omarchy ISO
installs it, install x11-wm/daemonarchy (Daemonarchy).
